I think I've solved it, at least until 3.5 or 5.0.  The "files"
directory in each package contains the FreeBSD patches for that port.
I've actually made three patches this time to go there, and they won't
get replaced unless someone breaks the naming rules and overwrites them.
One to comment out the rm -rf, one for Sir Hawk, and one for autopickup.

I just checked, and they all apply nicely to slashem as well.

In fact, I'd be surprised if they don't apply to future versions of
nethack.  When 35 or 40 is announced, I'll just make a directory of the
appropriate name--e.g., /usr/ports/games/nethack35/files--and copy them
there, with the rest of the port to come once available.

hawk

